                <pb facs="0609" n="589" sameAs="frus:frus1864p2/pg589"/>

                <head>Mr. Archibald to Lord Lyons.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">British Consulate</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">New York</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-04-07"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >April</hi> 7, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Lord:</hi> I have the honor to report to your
                    lordship that the persons whose names are mentioned in the subjoined list, and
                    who state themselves to be British subjects, are detained here as prisoners in
                    the county jail. The seven first-named persons were captured on board the
                    British steamer Scotia while on a voyage from Wilmington to Nassau. Two of them
                    report themselves to have been passengers in that vessel.</p>
                <p>The seven last-named persons were captured in the British steamer Don, of London,
                    while on a voyage from Nassau to Wilmington. One of them states himself to have
                    been a passenger on board the Don. The whole thirteen persons were lodged in the
                    county jail on the 25th ultimo. The Scotia was brought to this port for
                    adjudication, as reported in my despatch of the 9th ultimo. The Don was taken to
                    Boston. I see no reason for the detention of these prisoners here. I have caused
                    them to be examined by a clerk from this office, and believe them to be all
                    British subjects and entitled to British protection. There is likewise in the
                    county jail a British subject named Adolphus Russell, a native and resident of
                    Green Turtle Bay, Bahamas. He states himself to have been a passenger on board
                    the sloop Racer, of Green Turtle Bay, which was captured on the 1st of January
                    last and taken to Key West. Russell was kept on board the United States bark
                    Roebuck from the time of his capture until he was sent here and lodged in the
                    county jail, about three weeks since. He is suffering from ill health.</p>
                <pb facs="0610" n="590" xml:id="pg590"/>
                <p>Besides the above-mentioned persons, there is in the county jail, where he has
                    been imprisoned since the 2d of February last, a man named William Patterson,
                    master of the sloop Gopher, of Green Turtle Bay, Bahamas, which was captured and
                    sent to Key West on the 12th of December last. He states himself to be a native
                    of Denmark, is now of the age of forty-six years, and has resided twenty-eight
                    years in the Bahama islands, where he became naturalized as a British subject in
                    the year 1850.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <p rendition="#right">E. M. ARCHIBALD.</p>
